# Development workflow (S / M / L)

Before implementing non-trivial work, classify the change. **If unsure, ask the user** whether it is S, M, or L.

## Tiers

| Tier | When | Process |
|---|---|---|
| **S** | Bugfix, small polish, obvious one-file (or similarly tiny) change | Consult `AGENTS.md`, `CONTEXT.md`, and relevant ADRs/module READMEs. Grill only if real tradeoffs appear. Then implement. Suggest `/code-review` when done. |
| **M** | New behavior in a limited area, requirements need a written spec | Do **not** implement yet. Ask the user to run `/grill-with-docs`, then `/to-spec`, then `/implement`, then `/code-review`. |
| **L** | Cross-cutting work, `bwutils/` + `mod/` + signals, or new architecture | Same as M, plus `/to-tickets` (local `.scratch/`) after the spec and before `/implement`. |

## Skill invocation

Skills such as `/grill-with-docs`, `/to-spec`, `/to-tickets`, `/implement`, and `/code-review` are often `disable-model-invocation` — **do not improvise their full procedures**. Pause and ask the user to invoke the next skill. Local tickets/specs: see `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.

## Agent docs map maintenance

If you change how agent documentation is organized (`.cursor/rules`, `CONTEXT.md`, `docs/adr`, `docs/agents`, issue tracker choice, or this S/M/L workflow), **update `docs/agents/README.md` in the same change**.
